body.append(chapter(4,'Accounting fundamentals',
 h(2,'The accounting equation')+p('<strong>Assets = Liabilities + Equity.</strong> Assets are resources controlled by the business; liabilities are obligations; equity is the owners’ residual interest. Revenue increases profit and usually equity. Expenses reduce profit and equity.')+
 h(2,'Debit and credit reference')+table(['Account type','Normal balance','Increase','Decrease','Example'],[
('Asset','Debit','Debit','Credit','Bank, receivables, inventory'),('Liability','Credit','Credit','Debit','Payables, loans, tax due'),('Equity','Credit','Credit','Debit','Share capital, retained earnings'),('Revenue','Credit','Credit','Debit','Sales'),('Expense','Debit','Debit','Credit','Rent, wages, depreciation')])+
 h(2,'Double entry')+p('Every posted journal has equal total debits and credits. Northstar Trading Ltd invoices a customer £1,200: Debit Accounts Receivable £1,200; Credit Sales £1,200. Profit rises by £1,200 before related costs and tax, and the Balance Sheet shows a £1,200 receivable.')+
 h(2,'Accrual and cash accounting')+p('Accrual accounting recognises income when earned and expenses when incurred, regardless of payment. Cash accounting focuses on cash movement and may be acceptable only where applicable rules allow it. Ledgify’s invoice, bill and journal design is accrual-based.')+
 h(2,'Core terms')+ul(['<strong>Accounts receivable (AR):</strong> approved customer invoices less payments and credits.','<strong>Accounts payable (AP):</strong> approved supplier bills less payments and credits.','<strong>Trial Balance:</strong> account debit and credit totals at a date; it must balance.','<strong>General Ledger:</strong> detailed posted activity by account.','<strong>Financial period:</strong> reporting interval that may be open or locked.','<strong>Bank reconciliation:</strong> linking statement activity to ledger activity and explaining timing differences.','<strong>Depreciation:</strong> allocation of an asset’s depreciable cost across its useful life.','<strong>Cost of sales:</strong> cost assigned to goods sold; gross profit is sales less cost of sales.','<strong>Audit trail:</strong> who created, approved, posted, changed or reversed a record and when.'])+
 h(2,'VAT and tax')+p('RC1 includes country-neutral tax rates, periods, transactions and summary/preview pages. It does not perform electronic jurisdiction filing. “VAT” labels in the interface refer to transaction tax reporting; obtain professional advice before relying on a return.')+
 h(2,'Deletion, voiding and reversal')+p('Delete only unused drafts when the action is offered. Voiding changes a source document to a non-active state under its controlled rules. Reversal creates an offsetting accounting entry and preserves the original history. A reversed journal and its posted reversal remain visible in the ledger.')))

body.append(chapter(5,'Dashboard',
 p('Open <strong>Dashboard</strong> from the sidebar. It summarises connected financial information, recent invoices, recent transactions and cash-flow information. Cards and charts depend on the selected organisation and posted data.')+
 h(2,'Using the dashboard')+ol(['Confirm the organisation in the header.','Review summary cards and their dates.','Review Recent Invoices for overdue or unpaid items.','Review Recent Transactions for unusual values.','Use a card or linked item to open its detailed workflow where offered.'])+
 h(2,'Why dashboard and bank figures differ')+ul(['Approved invoices and bills affect profit and AR/AP before cash moves.','Unpresented payments and deposits create timing differences.','Statement rows may be imported but not reconciled.','Draft documents do not affect posted reports.','Date filters, foreign exchange rates, reversed entries or locked-period corrections may differ.'])+
 note('tip','Control','Use the Trial Balance, General Ledger and bank reconciliation—not dashboard cards alone—to substantiate period-end figures.')+shot('Figure 4. Dashboard summary cards, cash-flow chart and recent activity')))

body.append(chapter(6,'Sales and accounts receivable',
 h(2,'Customers')+p('Open <strong>Sales → Customers</strong> or <strong>Contacts → Customers</strong>. Use <strong>New Customer</strong> to enter identity and contact information. Open a customer to review summary cards, invoices, activity and statement; authorised users may edit details. Do not delete a customer with accounting history unless the workflow explicitly permits it.')+
 h(2,'Quotes and sales orders')+p('Open <strong>Sales → Quotes</strong> or <strong>Sales Orders</strong>. These commercial records do not recognise revenue merely by existing. Use supported detail actions to approve, convert, cancel or progress them. The new/edit route redirects to the integrated list workspace, so creation and editing occur there rather than on separate pages.')+
 h(2,'Create an invoice')+ol(['Open <strong>Sales → Invoices</strong> and choose <strong>New Invoice</strong>.','Select the customer.','Enter invoice date, due date, reference and currency shown by the form.','Add lines: description/product, quantity, unit price, income account and tax treatment where displayed.','Check subtotal, tax and total.','Save as draft. Review supporting evidence.','Approve when authorised. Approval posts the invoice.','Use the invoice details page to email, download or record payment where available.'])+
 h(2,'Invoice statuses')+table(['Status','Meaning','Permitted treatment'],[
('Draft','Saved but not posted.','Edit or delete if authorised.'),('Awaiting approval','Submitted for review.','Approver checks and approves or returns/corrects.'),('Approved','Posted and outstanding.','Do not freely edit; record payments or credits.'),('Partly paid','Some amount remains due.','Record only the remaining valid payment.'),('Paid','Nothing remains due.','No further payment allocation.'),('Void/Reversed','Controlled cancellation/correction.','Review the linked accounting history.')])+
 h(2,'Accounting entries')+table(['Event','Debit','Credit','Reports and balances'],[
('Approve £1,200 service invoice','Accounts Receivable £1,200','Sales £1,200','P&L revenue +£1,200; Balance Sheet AR +£1,200.'),('Receive £500','Bank £500','Accounts Receivable £500','AR falls to £700; bank rises £500; no new revenue.'),('Receive final £700','Bank £700','Accounts Receivable £700','AR becomes nil; invoice becomes Paid.'),('Approve credit/controlled reversal £1,200','Sales/returns £1,200','Accounts Receivable £1,200','Revenue and AR reduce, subject to tax and credit workflow.')])+
 h(2,'Payments and credits')+p('From Invoice Details or the eligible row action, select <strong>Record Payment</strong>, choose the bank account, enter payment date, amount, reference and optional notes, then confirm. An amount above the outstanding balance is rejected unless a specific credit workflow supports it. Credit Notes are under Sales and use draft, approval/application and void controls. Customer statements show invoices, payments, credits and running balance.')+
 note('warning','Posted sales','Never delete or edit an approved invoice to conceal a mistake. Use the available credit, void or reversal action and retain the reason and supporting documents.')+shot('Figure 5. Invoices list, New Invoice and Invoice Details')))

